        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/97f17d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-31T16:51:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Sefirit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e68b1a/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Sefirit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>DrScott wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Ronway wrote:<br><blockquote>&nbsp;Since he would also be redirecting that damage it would no longer be reduced so it'll go back to it's original value to the new target.&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nHmmm, that seems too good to be true. &nbsp;I'm not saying you're wrong, but that kind of seems like having it both ways. &nbsp;Wouldn't he also redirect 1 damage attacks by the same logic?\n</blockquote></div>\nRemember that when damage is redirected you start the attack over from the original attacker to the new target and recalculate any bonuses/negatives so the pipe wrench reduction no longer counts.&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Now this whole thing makes more sense - if I'd actually read the glassary I'd have learned that \"Damage that is redirected does not affect the oringinal target. &nbsp;Instead, it affects the target to whom it is directed.\"</p>",
